## CVE-2019-14897 port — summary

**Outcome:** candidate patch complete, uncommitted, preserved in an isolated worktree. Final orchestrator status is `blocked` because the validation gate is `partial` (no build infrastructure); no semantic defect was found.

### Mapping result
The reference fix targets `drivers/net/wireless/marvell/libertas/cfg.c`. The target `6d8764d3` (linux-3.16.y) predates the `f988d64010ec` "move under marvell vendor directory" rename, so the file lives at `drivers/net/wireless/libertas/cfg.c`. History tracing (model-led) showed:

- merge-base of target and reference is `19583ca` (Linux 3.16);
- target-side interval touches the file **0** times; blob `47a998d8f99e…` is identical at 3.16 and at the target;
- all vulnerable lines blame to 2010 commits and none of the 20 reference-side commits changes the anchors (`hits=0`);
- target/reference-parent diff has no hunk inside either vulnerable block.

### Applied fix (8 insertions, 1 file)
```c
/* add_ie_rates() */
+	if (ap_max > MAX_RATES) {
+		lbs_deb_assoc("invalid rates\n");
+		return tlv;
